node_modules/
# The same name without the slash, because a trailing slash matches directories
# ONLY and a `node_modules` **symlink** is not a directory to git. A fresh
# worktree has no deps, and linking them from the main checkout
# (`ln -s ../majorana/node_modules node_modules`) is the cheap way to run a
# checker there — after which `git add -A` stages the link as a tracked symlink,
# because the line above does not match it. Caught here 2026-08-11, one commit
# before it reached CI.
node_modules
.next/
# Alternate NEXT_DIST_DIR builds, so a second local dev server does not share
# (and corrupt) the first one's cache.
.next-*/
dist/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.env
.env.local
.env*.local
.turbo/
.vercel/
coverage/
report.json
.venv
.venv.nosync/
.DS_Store
bench/k6/out/

# The Leona plan tree lives in the PRIVATE repo EshMis/ai-ops (leona/plans/), and this
# path is a symlink to it. This repository is public and the tree includes
# plans/rebuild/05-security.md, which enumerates which security controls are built and
# which are not — owner ruling 2026-08-14.
#
# No trailing slash on purpose. `plans/` does NOT match a symlink named `plans`; git
# treats the entry as a directory pattern and the symlink is a file, so the ignore silently
# misses and the link gets committed.
/plans
